Michel Basquiat Memoriam explain my dear  countrymen at the moment that I speak to  you terrorist attacks of an  unprecedented level a happening in the  Paris Area there are dozens dead  there are many injured it's a horror we  have at my command mobilised all  possible forces so that we can  neutralize the terrorist threat and  secure all the areas that could be  affected I've also asked for military  reinforcements in the Paris Area to be  sure that another attack cannot take  place  I have also called a cabinet meeting  which will take place shortly two  decisions will be made a state of  emergency will be declared which means  that certain areas will be closed moving  through these areas will not be allowed  the state of emergency will be declared  throughout the country the second  decision I've made  it's the closure of the borders we must  be sure that nobody can enter to commit  whatever acts they may wish to and at  the same time that those who have  committed these crimes can be  apprehended if they are trying to leave  the country
 

